job.plain_text_description:
FIFA has established a Local FIFA Subsidiary in Brazil to work together with FIFA Zurich to deliver the biggest women’s sporting event in the world, the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™ (“FWWC2027”) that for the first time ever, is hosted in South America in Brazil. Now is your time to be part of the workforce that is creating this unique and unforgettable experience.

This is an exclusive job opportunity for people with disabilities, as part of our commitment to inclusive hiring.

Please submit your CV in English, as it will be reviewed by an international team.

Support the recruitment team in ensuring accurate and detail-oriented management of recruitment data, systems, and reporting tools, including spreadsheets, dynamic tables, and presentation materials that support hiring decisions, while attracting the best talents aligned with FWWC2027 values, conducting resume analysis and candidate screening.

Our selection process is accessible, and accommodations can be requested at any stage.

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES

- Data Management, Reporting & Analysis: Accurately input, update and maintain recruitment data across various systems and spreadsheets, ensuring precision and consistency;Build and maintain dynamic/pivot tables to organize and cross-reference recruitment data;Analyze recruitment reports and metrics, critically reviewing data to identify inconsistencies, trends and insights that support decision-making;Prepare clear and well-structured PowerPoint presentations to communicate recruitment data and updates to stakeholders;Update and standardize templates across systems;
- Manage recruitment systems, tools and templates with a high level of accuracy and attention to detail, maintaining up-to-date records of all recruitment information in alignment with internal stakeholders; hiring managers, workforce planning, onboarding and payroll;
- Analyze resumes, screen and shortlist candidates against role requirements, supporting the recruitment team throughout the end-to-end hiring process; sourcing, screening, interviewing, reference checks, offer support and onboarding;
- Provide support to functional areas and hiring managers about recruitment policies and procedures, clarifying recruitment processes, tools and workforce plan;
- Support employer branding actions, raising awareness about FWWC2027 and maximizing candidates' access to job advertisements;
- Comply with all FIFA and FWWC2027 hiring and recruitment policies and procedures and local legislation.

- Bachelor's degree completed or on going in Human Resources, Business Administration, Psychology or related field;
- Previous experience in recruitment processes, such as resume screening and candidate assessment, is a plus;
- Strong attention to detail and accuracy, particularly when working with spreadsheets and data entry; does not need to be an advanced Excel user, but must be highly reliable;
- Good working knowledge of HR/recruitment systems and applicant tracking systems;
- Proficiency in MS Excel, including building and interpreting pivot tables;
- Ability to prepare clear, well-organized PowerPoint presentations;
- Analytical mindset, able to review and critically assess data to support decision-making;
- Familiarity with employee administration and compliance requirements;
- Proactive and organized, able to work independently as well as part of a team;
- Knowledge of HR best practices, employment laws, and regulations;
- Strong communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills;
- Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion;
- Technology: Familiarity with MS Office tools (Excel, Word, PowerPoint) is desirable; prior exposure to HR systems and online collaboration tools will be considered a plus;
- Right to work in Brazil;
- Fluent in English (spoken and written);
- Fluent in Portuguese (spoken and written);
- Ability to re-locate to Rio de Janeiro.

FIFA has established a Local FIFA Subsidiary in Brazil to work together with FIFA Zurich to deliver the biggest women’s sporting event in the world, the FIFA Women’s World Cup 2027™ (“FWWC2027”) that for the first time ever, is hosted in South America in Brazil. Now is your time to be part of the workforce that is creating this unique and unforgettable experience.

Please submit your CV in English, as it will be reviewed by an international team.

FIFA has setup a fully owned Local Entity to deliver the ninth edition of the FIFA Women’s World Cup™, held in Brazil. The success and the growth of the competition depend on the ability and capabilities of the FIFA team to provide an enhanced experienced to all the key stakeholders linked to the tournament: fans and spectators following the event, participating teams and FIFA Commercial Partners.

Working alongside the FIFA/FIFA27 Partnership Rights Delivery (PRD) team and reporting to the FIFA Senior Partner Rights Delivery Manager in Zurich and the FIFA27 Senior F&B Concessions Manager, the F&B Concessions Manager is responsible for managing the operational planning and delivery readiness of the Public Food & Beverage (F&B) Concessions Programme across all official tournament stadiums. The objective is to implement and deliver successfully the FIFA Commercial Partners’ exclusive food & beverage rights.

The role is responsible for overseeing concessionaire operational planning, coordinating tournament deliverables, ensuring compliance with FIFA requirements, and supporting venue readiness activities. The F&B Concessions Manager acts as the primary operational interface between FIFA, appointed concessionaires, stadium authorities, and Host Football Associations (FAs) to ensure all operational requirements are planned, documented, and delivered according to FIFA timelines and standards.

The role does not hold responsibility for commercial negotiations, contractual management, menu approval, pricing strategy, Commercial Partner relationship management, or defining commercial rights delivery strategy, which remain under the responsibility of the Senior F&B Concessions Manager and FIFA Partnership Rights Delivery team.

Key responsibilities

- Manage appointed F&B Concessionaire(s) throughout the planning and delivery phases, monitoring compliance with FIFA requirements, project timelines and agreed operational deliverables;
- Manage the planning and implementation of the Public Food & Beverage Concessions Programme across all official tournament stadiums, ensuring operational readiness, consistency of delivery and compliance with FIFA requirements;
- Manage the operational implementation of the commercial rights granted to FIFA’s Commercial Partners within the F&B Concessions Programme, ensuring approved products, services and activation requirements are successfully integrated into stadium operations;
- Establish, implement and maintain operational procedures, controls, checklists and reporting mechanisms to support the successful delivery of the F&B Concessions Programme;
- Review, track and manage concessionaire deliverables, operational plans and readiness submissions, ensuring all requirements are delivered in accordance with FIFA standards and tournament deadlines;
- Coordinate the development and implementation of operational plans covering staffing, logistics, inventory management, food safety, sustainability, service delivery and contingency planning across all official stadiums;
- Develop and deliver training programmes, operational briefings and implementation guidelines for concessionaires, service providers and venue-based F&B resources;
- Oversee the review, mapping and optimization of F&B infrastructure, facilities and operational layouts within stadiums to support efficient service delivery and compliance with tournament requirements;
- Support the F&B Concessions team in the preparation and coordination of planning activities with FIFA Partnership Rights Delivery (Zurich) and other relevant FIFA functional areas to ensure alignment of operational and commercial objectives;
- Supervise the development and delivery of stadium F&B operations by appointed concessionaire(s), ensuring approved Commercial Partner requirements are implemented and stakeholder expectations are achieved;
- Manage operational relationships with appointed F&B Concessionaire(s), FIFA functional areas and venue stakeholders, ensuring effective communication, coordination and information flow throughout all tournament phases;
- Coordinate the reviewing and implementation of F&B operational signage elements, including menu boards and other concession-related branding and information materials, in collaboration with FIFA Partnership Rights Delivery and appointed concessionaires;
- Monitor stadium infrastructure and operational readiness delivery against established requirements, producing regular status reports, risk assessments and mitigation plans;
- Manage and coordinate the team of F&B Venue Managers, providing leadership, guidance and operational support across all official tournament venues;
- Support FIFA and FIFA27 Headquarters throughout tournament operations by consolidating venue reporting, monitoring operational performance, coordinating issue resolution and ensuring consistent implementation of FIFA standards across all stadiums;
- Oversee daily public F&B concession operations during the tournament, supporting the resolution of operational challenges and ensuring service levels and spectator experience objectives are achieved;
- Coordinate testing events, operational rehearsals and readiness exercises to validate concessionaire preparedness and support successful tournament delivery;
- Produce operational reports, readiness updates, post-event evaluations and lessons learned documentation to support decision-making and continuous improvement initiatives;
- Establish reporting procedures and communication protocols between venue-based F&B teams and FIFA27 Headquarters to ensure consistent implementation of operational standards across all venues.

- Minimum 4 years’ experience in the food and beverage, catering, or related professional area;
- Proven successful management and delivery of F&B concessions projects at major international and high-profile events, preferably in the sports industry;
- Advanced knowledge of the food & beverage concessions industry and preferably at football stadiums;
- Experience in major international sports / large-scale event management;
- Proven track record in managing complex projects, including overlay, preferably in the sports industry;
- Experience in project infrastructure management;
- Knowledge of basic utilities requirements, especially for food & beverage concessions (electricity, water supply, etc);
- Knowledge of food safety and hygienic requirements for food & beverage concessions operation;
- Knowledge and demonstrated ability in event planning and event project management, prioritize effectively, and work independently;
- Strong communication skills, both written and verbal;
- A team player, willing to work to tight timelines;
- Innovator and added-value approaches towards commercial rights delivery;
- Proficient in MS Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Visio & Project) planning software and online collaboration tools;
- Proven successful management and delivery of F&B concessions projects at major international and high-profile events, preferably in the sports industry;
- Advanced knowledge of the food & beverage concessions industry and preferably at football stadiums;
- Experience in major international sports / large-scale event management;
- Proven track record in managing complex projects, including overlay, preferably in the sports industry;
- Experience in project infrastructure management;
- Knowledge of basic utilities requirements, especially for food & beverage concessions (electricity, water supply, etc);
- Knowledge of food safety and hygienic requirements for food & beverage concessions operation;
- Knowledge and demonstrated ability in event planning and event project management, prioritize effectively, and work independently;
- Strong communication skills, both written and verbal;
- A team player, willing to work to tight timelines;
- Innovator and added-value approaches towards commercial rights delivery;
- Proficient in MS Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Visio & Project) planning software and online collaboration tools;
- Right to work in Brazil;
- Fluent in English (spoken and written);
- Fluent in Portuguese (spoken and written);
- Ability to re-locate to Rio de Janeiro.

The Rwanda Football Federation invites applications for the position of Technical Director. The appointee will lead football development across Rwanda and build connected pathways from grassroots participation to high performance for girls, boys, women and men in Rwanda.

- Develop, cost and implement a multi-year national technical development strategy aligned with FERWAFA priorities, FIFA and CAF programmes, and available resources; maintain clear annual targets and reporting.
- Lead grassroots and school football, youth development, talent identification, academies and regional pathways, with a deliberate transition into club and national team environments.
- Expand opportunities, qualified staffing and competition pathways for women and girls; embed inclusion, child safeguarding, welfare and integrity in every programme.
- Lead coach education, educator development, licensing pathways and continuing professional development; coordinate with refereeing, futsal, beach soccer and other technical units within their mandates now and in the future.
- Provide technical oversight and coordination for national team pathways, performance analysis, sports science and medical collaboration, respecting head coaches’ match and team selection responsibilities.
- Manage the technical department, plans, budgets, procurement inputs, partnerships, performance data and donor or FIFA and CAF programme reporting; work with clubs, leagues, schools, districts, ministries and international partners.

Essential:

- Substantial senior experience leading football development or comparable technical programmes;
- Demonstrated delivery of strategy across several age groups or levels; experience supervising teams and budgets;
- Credible knowledge of coach development and talent pathways;
- Commitment to women’s football, safeguarding and ethical leadership;
- Excellent written and spoken English and/or French;
- Ability to work in Rwanda or obtain appropriate authorization.
- A relevant university degree or recognized advanced football technical or coaching qualification is required.

FERWAFA will assess equivalent combinations of formal study and substantial technical leadership experience where its policy permits.

Desirable:

- FIFA or CAF technical leadership education;
- Advanced CAF, UEFA or equivalent coaching licenses or coach educator qualification;
- Experience in an association or multi-stakeholder national system;
- Fluency in either English or Kinyarwanda;
- Demonstrated work in African football.

These are advantages, not automatic exclusion criteria.

Submit:

- a cover letter explaining relevant results;
- a current CV;
- copies of key qualifications;
- a two-page vision for football development in Rwanda covering the first three years; and
- contact details for two professional referees.

Please indicate any actual or potential conflict of interest. Reference checks will be conducted only at the appropriate stage with candidate consent.

Selection and equal opportunity
Applications will be screened against the stated criteria, followed by a scored shortlist, a technical exercise, presentation and structured interview.

FERWAFA is committed to fair recruitment and welcomes qualified applicants regardless of sex, disability or background.
Candidates may request reasonable assessment accommodations through careers@ferwafa.com. Personal information will be used for recruitment and handled under
applicable privacy rules.

Send the complete application through FIFA Portal and/or careers@ferwafa.com by 20th November 2026 at 17h00’ (Kigali Time). Use the subject “Technical Director application
– Full name”.

FERWAFA will contact candidates selected for the next stage. No fee is charged for this recruitment.

job.html_description:
 The Academy Driver is responsible for providing a safe, reliable and professional driving service across. the Academy. Reporting to the Head of Academy Operations, the role includes, management of part-time drivers (exclusively Academy), and to work alongside the Club Driver &amp; Fleet Compliance Manager ensuring all vehicles are maintained and presented to a professional standard. The Academy Driver delivers a consistent, reliable service to ensure safe transport of Academy players, staff and guests.<br><br>This will be a part-time (20-hour) role, with hours split across a 7-day week.&nbsp;
<h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>Provide transport for identified registered players to and from our Motspur Park training site.</li><li>Provide transport for trialist players to and from airports, train stations, accommodation, and club activities.</li><li>Support the player induction process when identifying players in need of transport support.</li><li>Act as a guide for visits to Motspur Park and Craven Cottage.</li><li>Assist the club on 1st team match days for corporate driving requirement.</li><li>Support the Academy across key events and wider activities.</li><li>Promote the work of Fulham Academy amongst the London football community.</li><li>Always represent Fulham Football Club to a high standard in line with club values.</li></ul>
<h3>Requirements</h3><ul><li>Hold a full clean driving licence</li><li>Interact with others in a positive manner</li><li>Strong understanding of the local area</li><li>Positive ability to work within a diverse organisation</li><li>Self-starter who takes pride in the delivery of a professional service</li><li>Bi-Lingual (Desired)</li><li>D1 driving licence (Desired)</li></ul>

 Are you passionate about helping people lead healthier, more active lives? Do you want to make a meaningful difference by reducing social isolation, improving mental wellbeing, and creating opportunities for people to connect within their local community?<br><br>If so, Fulham FC Foundation would love to hear from you.<br><br>We are seeking an enthusiastic, motivated, and committed Health &amp; Wellbeing Coach to join our team on a 20 hour per week contract. Reporting to the Health &amp; Wellbeing Manager, you will play a vital role in delivering high-quality sport, physical activity, and wellbeing programmes that positively influence people of all ages across our local communities.<br><br>Through your work, you will help participants improve their physical health and mental wellbeing, build confidence, and develop meaningful social connections. Our programmes use the power of sport and physical activity as a vehicle to create lasting change, with a focus on supporting healthier lifestyles and stronger, more connected communities.<br><br>As a Health &amp; Wellbeing Coach, you will deliver a range of community-based activities designed to improve physical health, reduce loneliness and isolation, and support positive mental wellbeing. You will also work closely with local partners and stakeholders, helping to ensure our programmes deliver meaningful outcomes that extend beyond participation in sport and physical activity.<br><br>The successful candidate will have experience delivering football, sport, physical activity, or health improvement programmes within community settings, hold a minimum FA Introduction to Coaching Football (Level 1 equivalent) qualification, and demonstrate a strong commitment to the values and charitable mission of Fulham FC Foundation.<br><br>Our Health &amp; Wellbeing programmes are delivered across Lambeth, Merton, Hammersmith &amp; Fulham, Wandsworth, and Kingston. Sessions take place primarily on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Fridays, so we are looking for an individual who can travel independently across these boroughs and is available to work on these days.<br><br>Why Join Fulham FC Foundation?<br><br>At Fulham FC Foundation, we are committed to using the power of sport to transform lives and strengthen communities. By joining our team, you will:<br>• &nbsp;Work alongside a highly experienced, passionate, and supportive delivery team,<br>• &nbsp;Access a range of training and professional development opportunities,<br>• &nbsp;Continue to develop your coaching, facilitation, and community engagement skills,<br>• &nbsp;Play a key role in delivering life-changing programmes across South West London,<br>• &nbsp;Make a genuine difference to the lives of people within our local communities.<br>We strive for service excellence in everything we do and set high standards for all staff representing the Foundation. In return, we provide a supportive and inclusive environment where you can grow professionally while making a real and lasting impact on the people and communities we serve.<br><br><strong><u>Further Information</u></strong><br id="isPasted">Salary range is £13,500 - £14,000 for 20 hours per week.<br><br>Closing date for applications is 5.00pm on Friday 30th October 2026.<br><br>First stage interviews will take place in person on Friday 13th November at Craven Cottage. Please ensure you are available to interview on this date prior to applying.<br><br>Second stage interviews will be organised with individual candidates following the completion of the first stage interviews.<br>&nbsp;
<h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>To act as an Ambassador for Fulham FC Foundation (FFCF), representing the organisation professionally in line with its values.</li><li>To plan and deliver high-quality sessions to children, young people &amp; adults in-line with FFCF standards.</li><li>To provide a safe, positive and inclusive environment at all times,</li><li>To adhere to FFCF’s safeguarding policies and procedures, ensuring the timely reporting of any safeguarding concerns or incidents within sessions.</li><li>To engage, include, inspire and grow participation across FFCF health &amp; wellbeing activities.</li><li>To support the transition of participants between different FFCF programmes and activities.</li><li>To champion opportunities for individuals from underrepresented groups within FFCF activities.&nbsp;</li><li>To support the development of FFCF programmes through positive collaboration with internal departments and colleagues.&nbsp;</li><li>To support the promotion of all FFCF programmes across the local community.&nbsp;</li><li>To assist in data collection and completion of monitoring &amp; evaluation on an ongoing basis.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br><em>*This job description should not be regarded as exclusive or exhaustive. It is intended as an outline indication of areas of activity and responsibility and will be amended in the light of the changing needs of the organisation.</em>
<h3>Requirements</h3><strong><u>Essential:&nbsp;</u></strong><br><strong>Experience:&nbsp;</strong><br><ul><li>Has experience delivering sport, physical activity, or health and wellbeing programmes within community settings</li></ul><br><strong>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:</strong><br><ul><li>Has a proven track record of maintaining the highest standards of safeguarding, health and safety, and quality assurance</li><li>Understands the importance of inclusion, participant welfare, and community engagement</li><li>Introduction to Coaching Football qualification</li><li>Base knowledge of and willingness to learn &amp; contribute towards FFCF strategic aims.</li></ul><br><strong>Personal Qualities:</strong><br><ul><li>Shares our commitment to creating positive outcomes for participants and communities.</li><li>A positive role model.</li><li>Ability to travel independently across South-West London, including transport of equipment.</li><li>Well presented, with a professional manner.</li><li>Positive, energetic persona. Able to build rapport with participants.</li><li>Excellent time-keeping &amp; punctuality.<ul><li>Willingness to learn &amp; develop personally &amp; professionally.</li><li>Demonstrates excellent communication and relationship-building skills</li></ul></li></ul>&nbsp;<br><strong><u>Preferred:&nbsp;<br></u>Experience:&nbsp;</strong><br><ul><li>Working with vulnerable adults</li><li>Working for a Club Community Organisation (CCO).</li><li>Marketing &amp; promoting participation activities in the community.</li><li>Delivery of sport or health &amp; wellbeing activities specifically to females.</li></ul><br><strong>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:</strong><br><ul><li>FA Level 2/UEFA C in Coaching Football qualification (or higher).</li><li>Additional PE/HLTA qualification</li><li>Non-football NGB sports qualifications.</li><li>In-date FA Emergency First Aid (or willingness to work towards)</li><li>In-date FA Safeguarding Children certificate (or willingness to work towards)</li></ul>

job.plain_text_description:
Fulham FC is looking for an ambitious and analytical CRM Marketing Manager to play a key role in delivering the Club’s wider digital and data growth strategy.

As guardian of the Club’s fan database, you will provide actionable insight and reporting to assist the Club in making informed decisions which support revenue generation across a range of commercial products, drive supporter engagement and acquisition.

The CRM Marketing Manager will own the the development of multichannel CRM marketing plans, audience segmentation and automated workflows, with the aim of serving existing fans and attracting new audiences with more personalised content and relevant experiences.

Working across the Club’s digital estate, the role will be responsible for tracking user journeys, assess UX and improve conversion rates across owned and paid media chanels.

You will work closely with internal stakeholders to ensure MarTech/CRM tools are effectively integrated, optimised, and evolved across the business, enabling us to maximise our understanding of the Fulham fan, align on business priorities and support growth.

Responsibilities

This role leads the management and development of CRM marketing tools and fan audience data, driving campaigns to support multiple departments including but not limited to marketing, ticketing, hospitality, retail and Fulham FC partners.

Responsibilities include:

• Develop and deliver the Club’s fan data strategy focused on fan acquisition, engagement/retention, and commercial performance;

• Ownership of the Fulham fan database and management of appointed MarTech/CRM systems and tools, including oversight for data integrations and hygiene;

• Lead on supporter base insights, key market segments and KPIs; being a source of truth for FFC fan data, providing regular reporting on data size, quality and profiling, as well as recommendations for key target markets/potential commercial and acquisition opportunities;

• Design, create and deploy automated, personalised and triggered multi-channel CRM marketing campigns – including audience segmentation, channel recommendations, execution and analysis: ensuring the right audiences are targeted with the right message across the right channel, at the right time;

• Lead on data growth initiatives across all club touchpoints; track performance and adopt a ‘test and learn’ approach to improve acquisition/conversion, maximise communication effectiveness and reduce friction to further engagement;

• Oversight of daily commercial sales to understand performance, run-rates and gaps, providing reccomendations to support growth;

• Be a key support to the hospitality sales teams, implementing tools and features within CRM that improve efficiency and provide insight across sales and marketing, measuring the value of campaigns and support pipeline management;

• Lead on Club audience research (e.g., surveys, focus groups);

• Ensure marketing technology platforms are fully aligned with the Club’s broader data and technology ecosystem, working with the team to strengthen data insights;

• Maintain the quality and integrity of customer data through regular audits, data cleaning, and deduplication processes.

Requirements

The CRM Marketing Manager must:

• Demonstrable experience working in CRM, marketing or lifecycle marketing, with a strong track record of delivering effective campaigns and commercial success;

• Be comfortable working with large quantities of customer data and building audiences with MarTech/CRM tools;

• Be confident to own CRM marketing activity from planning through to review and performance analytics;

• Possess strong analytical skills, feeding actionable insight back to the business in a timely and accurate manner;

• Be experienced in data segmentation and working across different channels, including email, SMS, app/push, website and paid media;

• Be adaptable, organised and able to manage several projects at once;

• Strong understanding of GDPR and UK data protection requirements;

• Have a high attention to detail;

• Excellent written and verbal communication skills – able to build strong relationships to work with internal and external stakeholders/suppliers.

Ideally, the CRM Marketing Manager will:

• Have experiences of implementing/activating a CDP/CDXP system;

• Have experience of using DotDigital or an equivalent MarTech/email platform;

• Be experienced in managing user journeys across a single sign on (SSO) solution;

• Be competent using Google Analytics;

• Have experience of Microsoft Dynamics.

job.html_description:
 Oversee the efficient receipt, storage, dispatch and movements of all stock. Be able to ensure productivity targets are achieved and that all warehouse processes are running smoothly and promptly. Delivering of Stock to the store.&nbsp;<br><br>This role is 24 hours per week: shifts on Monday, Tuesday and Friday.&nbsp;
<h3>Responsibilities</h3>Below are example responsibilities but this is not intended to be an exhaustive list:<br><ul><li>Driving between sites to deliver retail stock as and when required.</li><li>Control retail stock movements</li><li>Responsible for pick, pack and dispatch in the online retail store.</li><li>Ensure product is stored in a safe and responsible manner.</li><li>Support Retail team in all aspects of stock and movements.</li><li>Support internet and online team.</li><li>Strategically manage warehouse in compliance with company’s policies and vision</li><li>Implement and adhere to all Club procedures ensuring all staff are fully aware and always trained</li><li>Uphold all retail security procedures, working closely with the Warehouse team</li><li>Support and reflect the Club Values on a day-to-day basis, ensuring the team are also demonstrating the appropriate behaviours</li><li>Proactively seek to build and maintain relationships with appropriate people in the business, and build the profile of the retail operation</li></ul><br><strong><u>Key Skills:</u></strong><br><ul><li>A strong communication skill at all levels both oral and written</li><li>Strong interpersonal skills and confidence in dealing with people at all levels of the organisation</li><li>Pragmatic and flexible approach</li><li>Work well under pressure through very busy trading periods</li><li>Team player with a hands-on approach</li><li>Know how to do Shirt printings&nbsp;</li><li>The ability to drive a van for delivery purposes</li></ul><br>&nbsp;
<h3>Requirements</h3><strong><u>Essential:</u></strong><br><br><strong>Experience:</strong><br>· Retail Systems<br>· Administrative background<br>· Driving – full clean driving licence<br><br><strong>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:</strong><br>· GCSE level Educated<br>· PC literate<br><br><strong>Personal Qualities:</strong><br>· Enthusiastic and creative<br>· Reliable And Dedicated<br>· Respect for confidentiality<br>· Flexible attitude to work tasks<br><br><strong><u>Preferred:</u></strong><br><br><strong>Experience:</strong><br>· Retail Product Knowledge<br>&nbsp;· Online Retail Skills<br>&nbsp;· Retail Operations environment&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;· Shirt Printing<br><br><strong>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:&nbsp;</strong><br>· Retail software / system

 Fulham FC Foundation are currently seeking to recruit an enthusiastic and committed person to take up the casual position of DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coach.<br><br>Reporting directly to our Senior DisAbility Development Manager, the DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coaches are responsible for delivering high-quality football &amp; sports coaching to children, young people and adults with disabilities and additional needs. This role involves delivery across a wide-range of our DisAbility Programmes, including Pan DisAbility Clubs, Active Autism, Down’s Syndrome ‘Badgers’, Blind and Partially Sighted, Cerebral Palsy and Dwarfism Football Sessions. In addition there will be opportunities to work in our DisAbility Schools programme delivering PE, Enrichment Activities and After School Clubs.<br><br>While the primary focus of this role is on DisAbility Football &amp; Sport, there may be opportunities to contribute to other FFC Foundation activities such as Skills Club, Development Centres, Soccer Schools, Primary Education, Kicks, and Health &amp; Wellbeing. We would encourage candidates to prioritise DisAbility Programmes where possible, while remaining flexible to support other areas as needed.<br><br>This is a casual role where flexibility is essential, as the role necessitates involvement in supporting the delivery of programme activities as and when required. &nbsp;<br><br>The successful candidate will be somebody who has prior experience delivering football &amp; sports coaching sessions to children &amp; young people with disabilities or additional needs in grassroots &amp; school settings, holds at least a FA Level 1/Introduction to Coaching Football qualification and is committed to the charitable purpose of Fulham FC Foundation.<br><br>As this role is casual, there is no set timetable. Sessions may be offered on an adhoc or regular basis, depending on the needs of Fulham FC Foundation. It is the responsibility of the DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coaches to maintain consistent and effective communication with our Senior DisAbility Development Manager and Operations Officers to ensure the continuation of work.<br><br>Whilst there is no obligation for Fulham FC Foundation to provide, or for the DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coaches to accept, work. DisAbility Football &amp; Sports Coaches who do not work for an extended period of time, will be deactivated.<br><br>The successful candidates should be available to work across at least one of the below times, in order to receive work. We are extremely keen to hear from those who are able to work on Saturday mornings.<br><br>Weekdays – 9am to 5 pm;<br>Weekday Evenings – 5pm to 9pm<br>Weekends – Saturdays – 8am to 12noon.<br>Work in other timings is available, however on a far reduced frequency.<br>Salary Range: £12.95 p/h to £16.50 p/h<br><br><strong>Next steps</strong>:<br>There is no closing date for this role. Applications will be reviewed on a bi-weekly basis.<br><br><strong>If successful, you will join a vibrant team who are passionate about achieving the organisation's vision of “an active, inclusive and thriving community”, and you’ll have the opportunity to build on your existing skills through a variety of training and development opportunities and experiences</strong><br>*<strong>This job description should not be regarded as exclusive or exhaustive. It is intended as an outline indication of areas of activity and responsibility and will be amended in the light of the changing needs of the organisation</strong>.
<h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>To act as an Ambassador for Fulham FC Foundation (FFCF), representing the organisation professionally in line with its values.</li><li>To plan and deliver high-quality football and sports coaching sessions to children, young people &amp; adults in-line with FFCF standards.</li><li>To provide a safe, positive and inclusive learning environment at all times,</li><li>To adhere to FFCF’s safeguarding policies and procedures, ensuring the timely reporting of any safeguarding concerns or incidents within sessions.</li><li>To engage, include, inspire and grow participation across FFCF activities.</li><li>To support the transition of participants between different FFCF programmes and activities.</li><li>To champion opportunities for individuals from underrepresented groups within FFCF activities.&nbsp;</li><li>To identify and support progression pathways for talented young people.&nbsp;</li><li>To support the development of FFCF programmes through positive collaboration with Department Managers / Operations Officers.&nbsp;</li><li>To support the promotion of FFCF programmes across the local community.</li><li>&nbsp;To assist in data collection and completion of monitoring &amp; evaluation on an ongoing basis.</li></ul>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;
<h3>Requirements</h3>Essential:<br>Experience:<br><ul><li>Delivery of football coaching sessions in a grassroots environment</li><li>Delivery of sports coaching sessions to children, young people or adults with disabilities and additional needs.</li><li>Delivery within a school/college setting.</li><li>Working in a customer-facing role.</li></ul><br>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:<br><ul><li>Introduction to Coaching Football qualification</li><li>In-date FA Emergency First Aid</li><li>In-date FA Safeguarding Children certificate</li><li>Base knowledge of and willingness to learn &amp; contribute towards FFCF strategic aims.</li></ul><br>Personal Qualities:<br><ul><li>A positive role-model for children &amp; young people.</li><li>Ability to travel independently across South-West London, including transport of equipment.</li><li>Well presented, with a professional manner.</li><li>Positive, energetic persona. Able to build rapport with participants.</li><li>Excellent time-keeping &amp; punctuality.</li><li>Willingness to learn &amp; develop personally &amp; professionally.</li></ul><br>Preferred:<br>Experience:<br><ul><li>Delivery of football &amp; sports coaching sessions in a Club Community Organisation (CCO).</li><li>Delivery of Physical Education within a school setting.</li><li>Delivery within a classroom environment.</li><li>Marketing &amp; Promoting participation activities in the community.</li><li>Delivery of football &amp; sports coaching sessions to females.</li></ul><br>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:<br><ul><li>FA Level 2/UEFA C in Coaching Football qualification (or higher).</li><li>Additional PE/HLTA qualification</li><li>Mentoring qualification</li><li>Non-football NGB sports qualifications.</li></ul>

 The Video &amp; Content Officer will be responsible for creating compelling visual content that showcases the impact of Fulham FC Foundation's work. The role will lead on videography and &nbsp;content creation across the Foundation's programmes, events and campaigns. &nbsp;<br><br>Working closely with delivery teams and the Communications Manager, the postholder will &nbsp;capture and share engaging stories that increase participation, attract supporters and partners, &nbsp;and demonstrate community impact.<br><br>Why Join Fulham FC Foundation?<br><br>At Fulham FC Foundation, we are committed to using the power of sport to transform lives and strengthen communities. By joining our team, you will:<br>• &nbsp;Work alongside a highly experienced, passionate, and supportive delivery team,<br>• &nbsp;Access a range of training and professional development opportunities,<br>• &nbsp;Continue to develop your coaching, facilitation, and community engagement skills,<br>• &nbsp;Play a key role in delivering life-changing programmes across South West London,<br>• &nbsp;Make a genuine difference to the lives of people within our local communities.<br>We strive for service excellence in everything we do and set high standards for all staff representing the Foundation. In return, we provide a supportive and inclusive environment where you can grow professionally while making a real and lasting impact on the people and communities we serve.<br><br><strong><u>Further Information</u></strong><br>Salary range is £27,000 - £28,500 for 40 hours per week.<br>​<br>Please note: closing date for applications is 25th October.<br><br><br><br><br>&nbsp;
<h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>To act as an Ambassador for Fulham FC Foundation (FFCF), representing the organisation professionally in line with its values.</li></ul><br><strong>Videography and Content Production&nbsp;</strong><br>• Plan, capture and edit video content for promotional, fundraising, programme and impact &nbsp;campaigns. &nbsp;<br>• Produce engaging short-form and long-form video content suitable for digital and social media &nbsp;platforms.&nbsp;<br>• Develop creative concepts and storyboards aligned with campaign objectives.<br>• Support regular video review and planning meetings to ensure content quality and consistency. &nbsp;<br><br><strong>Storytelling and Impact Content&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;<br>• Lead the planning, filming, editing and delivery of participant case study videos. &nbsp;<br>• Work directly with programme teams and beneficiaries to identify compelling stories. &nbsp;<br>• Ensure all content is captured and produced in line with safeguarding, consent and brand &nbsp;guidelines. &nbsp;<br><br><strong>Photography &nbsp;</strong><br>• Support on the capture of high-quality photography from Foundation programmes, events, &nbsp;campaigns and community activities. &nbsp;<br>• Maintain a comprehensive library of images for future communications and marketing use.&nbsp;<br>• Edit and optimise photographic content for digital, print and social media channels. &nbsp;<br><br><strong>Marketing Support&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;<br>• Provide ad hoc multimedia and creative support for communications and marketing campaigns. &nbsp;• Assist with content requirements for fundraising, events and partnership activations.<br><br><br><br>&nbsp;<br><em>*This job description should not be regarded as exclusive or exhaustive. It is intended as an outline indication of areas of activity and responsibility and will be amended in the light of the changing needs of the organisation.</em>
<h3>Requirements</h3><strong><u>Essential:&nbsp;</u></strong><br><strong>Experience:&nbsp;</strong><br>• Experience in professional videography and photography. &nbsp;<br>• Experience producing content for social media, websites and digital marketing campaigns. &nbsp;<br>• Experience editing video and photographic assets. &nbsp;<br>• Experience interviewing and developing feature videos.&nbsp;<br><br><strong>Skills, Knowledge &amp; Qualifications:</strong><ul><li>Proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud applications, including Premiere Pro, Photoshop and &nbsp;Lightroom. &nbsp;</li><li>Strong storytelling and content-writing skills. &nbsp;</li><li>Excellent planning and organisational abilities. &nbsp;</li><li>Ability to work independently while managing multiple projects. &nbsp;</li><li>Strong interpersonal skills and confidence when engaging with programme participants.&nbsp;</li></ul><br><strong>Desirable</strong><ul><li>Experience within sport, education, youth work, charity or community sectors. &nbsp;</li><li>Knowledge of social media content trends and platform best practice.&nbsp;</li><li>Understanding of safeguarding and consent processes when working with children and &nbsp;vulnerable adults.</li></ul>
